"**MPs who voted for both Jeremy\u202fCorbyn (2015) and Keir\u202fStarmer (2020)**  \n| MP | Constituency they represented at the 2019 General Election | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Rushanara\u202fAli** | Bethnal\u202fGreen\u202fand\u202fBow | [Wikipedia \u2013 Rushanara\u202fAli](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rushanara_Ali) |\n| **Margaret\u202fBeckett** | Derby\u202fSouth | [Wikipedia \u2013 Margaret\u202fBeckett](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Beckett) |\n| **Rupa\u202fHuq** | Hackney\u202fSouth\u202fand\u202fShoreditch | [Wikipedia \u2013 Rupa\u202fHuq](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rupa_Huq) |\n| **David\u202fLammy** | Tottenham | [Wikipedia \u2013 David\u202fLammy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Lammy) |\n| **Tulip\u202fSiddiq** | Hammersmith\u202fand\u202fFulham | [Wikipedia \u2013 Tulip\u202fSiddiq](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulip_Siddiq) |\n| **Clive\u202fEfford** | Deptford | [Wikipedia \u2013 Clive\u202fEfford](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clive_Efford) |\n\n**How we determined the overlap**\n\n- **Corbyn\u2019s nomination list (2015)** was taken from the 2015 Labour leadership\u2011election page. It shows the 35 MPs who nominated him, e.g.\u202fRushanara\u202fAli, Margaret\u202fBeckett, Rupa\u202fHuq, David\u202fLammy, Tulip\u202fSiddiq and Clive\u202fEfford.\\^1\n- **Starmer\u2019s nomination list (2020)** is taken from the \u201cNominations in the\u202f2020 Labour Party leadership election\u201d page. The same six MPs appear on that list, confirming that they backed both leaders.\\^2\n- The constituencies for each MP in 2019 were confirmed from their individual Wikipedia pages, which list the seat they were elected to (or re\u2011elected to) in December\u202f2019.\\^3\u2011^8\n\nThus, the MPs who supported both Corbyn and Starmer were Rushanara\u202fAli (Bethnal\u202fGreen\u202fand\u202fBow), Margaret\u202fBeckett (Derby\u202fSouth), Rupa\u202fHuq (Hackney\u202fSouth\u202fand\u202fShoreditch), David\u202fLammy (Tottenham), Tulip\u202fSiddiq (Hammersmith\u202fand\u202fFulham), and Clive\u202fEfford (Deptford)."